description:
A line spends bought time without a payment per call. Time burns only while a call runs on the line; calls at once burn once. A websocket subscription at /rpc/<chain> is a running call: it burns every millisecond it is open, idle gaps included, until you unsubscribe or the time runs out. {"op":"off"}: no new calls; a running call burns to its end. op: open {channelId} returns a message to sign with the payer key; prove {channelId, nonce, signature} returns the credential; on, off, status, close {credential}.
Free. Opens, switches and closes a line on your channel. open returns a message; sign it with the payer key; prove returns the credential calls carry.
Example: {"op":"open","channelId":"<your channel id>"}
